<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The native part of a plain-FrameLayout ad slot: AdsController.slot() inflates it into the screen's
    container when the console turns <slot>_native on (an AdSlotView carries its own parts instead).
    The gutter and the vertical gap live on this root, not in the host, so there is one place to change them for every screen in the app.
    That is why this file uses @dimen/_*sdp rather than the raw dp the rest of the bundle uses -
    a project adopting this package needs the sdp library as well as the serialization plugin.

    It starts GONE and stays GONE unless an ad is actually shown: NativeAdLoader sets it VISIBLE
    when a request goes out and back to GONE when the slot is disabled or the ad fails. A screen whose
    <screen>_<position>_native is 0 - which is what DEFAULT_JSON ships - therefore measures exactly as it did
    before the slot was added, and a scrolling screen keeps its old clearance: the host constrains its
    scroll container's bottom to this slot's top with layout_goneMarginBottom, which resolves back to
    the parent's bottom while the slot is gone.

    The shimmer is the whole of layout_banner_ad_shimmer_placeholder's native counterpart, included
    rather than copied: NativeAdLoader expects the slot to arrive holding the layout 1 skeleton
    and swaps in the one for layouts 2..5 when the console asks for those, so the two must not drift.
    Both heights are wrap_content - unlike the banner the native is not resized in code, it is
    whichever of the five layouts the console picked.

    **The gap above and below the ad is here, not in the host.** An ad has to read as clearly
    separate from the app's own content, and on a scrolling screen it does not: the content scrolls
    right up to the slot's edge and the two read as one column. The padding on this root - 14sdp either side, 4sdp top and bottom - is that
    separation, and it belongs to the package for two reasons. It is the same gap on every screen,
    so a host that has to add it per slot will sooner or later miss one. And it is free: the loaders
    collapse *this* view, so the padding exists only while an ad is actually showing - a screen whose
    flag is 0 measures exactly as it did before, with no gone-margin bookkeeping on the host side.

    Both edges, because a slot does not know which way it faces. The same include is the top slot on
    one screen, the bottom slot on another and a mid slot between two blocks of content on a third,
    so "the content-facing edge" is not a thing this file can know.

    The gutter is here for the same reason, and it is the one place the package spends a dependency
    to get it: `@dimen/_14sdp` means a project adopting this bundle needs com.intuit.sdp as well as
    the serialization plugin. One place to change every slot's spacing was judged worth that. A
    project without `sdp` swaps these four values for raw dp - they are the only four in the bundle.

    ADS BUNDLE FILE. It follows the package's conventions, not the host project's: the ad_* colours
    from colors_ads.xml and the bundle's layout_ prefix. The four `@dimen/_*sdp` above are the one
    exception to the bundle's raw-dp rule, and they are the whole of the package's `sdp`
    requirement - see the paragraph above.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/adSlotNativeRoot"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:paddingStart="@dimen/_14sdp"
    android:paddingEnd="@dimen/_14sdp"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/_4sdp"
    android:paddingBottom="@dimen/_4sdp"
    android:visibility="gone"
    tools:visibility="visible"
    tools:ignore="MergeRootFrame">
    <!--
        Not a <merge>, which is what lint suggests: this root is the slotRoot the loaders
        hold and set VISIBLE or GONE. NativeAdLoader collapses the slot by setting exactly
        this view GONE, so it has to survive inflation as a view of its own. A <merge> would
        put its children straight into the host screen with nothing left to collapse.
    -->

    <include
        android:id="@+id/shimmerNativeAd"
        layout="@layout/layout_native_ad_shimmer_placeholder" />

    <FrameLayout
        android:id="@+id/containerNativeAd"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

</FrameLayout>
